          "Social-Network Similarity Notes": "High local clustering and short paths, but comparatively narrow degrees."
        },
        {
          "Model": "Barabasi-Albert scale-free",
          "Nodes": 30,
          "Edges": 56,
          "Density": 0.12873563218390804,
          "Average Degree": 3.7333333333333334,
          "Average Clustering": 0.3001960784313725,
          "Connected": true,
          "Connected Components": 1,
          "Average Shortest Path": 2.1816091954022987,
          "Path Length Scope": "whole graph",
          "Maximum Degree": 18,
          "Degree Standard Deviation": 3.5207322470695717,
          "Social-Network Similarity Notes": "Strong hubs and heterogeneous degrees, but weaker local clustering here."
        }
      ],
      "conclusion": "Watts-Strogatz captures clustering and short paths; Barabasi-Albert captures hubs and heterogeneous degree. A social network can require both properties, so no model is universally best."
